.TH LINEAR 1 2000-1月 "set_baseline" "set_baseline"
.SH NAME
set_baseline \- Set the wildtype baseline (the cell context) of the perturbation engine.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIset_baseline(\fBmodel\fR as <generic> ElasticNet, 
\fBgenes\fR as any, 
\fBvalues\fR as any, 
[\fB<Environment>\fR]);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Set the wildtype baseline (the cell context) of the perturbation engine.
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBmodel\fB \fR\- the perturbation engine that is created via \fBelastic_model\fR. 
.PP
.PP
\fBgenes\fB \fR\- 
 the gene ids of the given expression profile, the matching against the model is
 case insensitive and the genes that are not modelled are ignored.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBvalues\fB \fR\- 
 the baseline expression values, they must be in the model space (i.e. the same
 transformation that was used to fit the network, for example \fBlog2(CPM + 1)\fR).
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBenv\fB \fR\- the R# runtime environment object. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
the number of the genes that have been matched and written
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
linear
.SH FILES
.PP
TRNtoolkit.dll
.PP
